WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
By now you're most likely
familiar with the basics of

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.530
databases and you
might even have

3
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.095
come across some
simple SQL syntax.

4
00:00:07.095 --> 00:00:10.620
Why do developers use SQL
to interact with databases?

5
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.750
SQL is a popular
language choice for

6
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.825
databases because of the many
advantages that it offers.

7
00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:17.625
Now for the next few minutes,

8
00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:20.910
you'll identify the
advantages of SQL and

9
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.530
demonstrate how
the advantages of

10
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.930
SQL assist with database tasks.

11
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.970
SQL is the interface or

12
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.310
bridge between a
relational database and

13
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.650
its users and offers
web developers

14
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.295
a wide range of advantages.
Let's look at a few of them.

15
00:00:35.295 --> 00:00:37.440
The biggest advantage
of SQL is that it

16
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.990
requires very little
coding skills to use,

17
00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.850
is just a set of keywords.

18
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.970
There aren't many lines
of code required to

19
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.220
perform basic CRUD operations,

20
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.530
or add, create, update,

21
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.705
and delete tasks
on the database.

22
00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:54.055
It's a very developer or
user-friendly language.

23
00:00:54.055 --> 00:00:57.050
SQL's interactivity
makes it even more

24
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.240
user-friendly because
it lets developers

25
00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.155
write complex queries in
a short space of time.

26
00:01:02.155 --> 00:01:04.130
If you need to work
with relational

27
00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.840
databases for your next project,

28
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.185
you just need to know what
keywords to use and when.

29
00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:12.140
SQL is also a standard
language that can be used

30
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.140
with all relational
databases like MySQL.

31
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.970
This also means that
there's a lot of

32
00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.370
support and
information available.

33
00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.785
SQL can run on any computer

34
00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:24.260
once you've database
software installed.

35
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.890
SQL is also a portable language.

36
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.535
Once you write your code,

37
00:01:28.535 --> 00:01:30.650
it can then be used
in any hardware,

38
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.315
on any operating system or
platform wherever you need.

39
00:01:34.315 --> 00:01:36.815
If you write SQL
code in a desktop

40
00:01:36.815 --> 00:01:39.485
and then move it to a
production server environment,

41
00:01:39.485 --> 00:01:42.235
it will run the same
in both locations.

42
00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.200
Also, SQL is a
comprehensive language that

43
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.455
covers all areas of database
management administration.

44
00:01:48.455 --> 00:01:50.195
For example, it allows you to

45
00:01:50.195 --> 00:01:52.730
create databases,
insert, update,

46
00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.430
and delete data,
retrieve and share data

47
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.580
among multiple users and
manage database security.

48
00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.180
This is made possible
through subsets of SQL like

49
00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.635
DDL or Data Definition
Language, DML,

50
00:02:05.635 --> 00:02:07.955
also known as Data
Manipulation Language,

51
00:02:07.955 --> 00:02:10.595
DQL or Data Query Language,

52
00:02:10.595 --> 00:02:14.360
and DCL, also known as
Data Control Language.

53
00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.150
The final advantage of
SQL is that it lets

54
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.190
database users
process large amounts

55
00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.460
of data quickly and efficiently.

56
00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.915
You now know that
SQL is a simple,

57
00:02:23.915 --> 00:02:26.345
standard, portable,
comprehensive,

58
00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.070
and efficient language
that can be used to

59
00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:31.105
communicate and work with
relational databases.

60
00:02:31.105 --> 00:02:35.210
You're well on your way to
mastering SQL. Well done.